\textbf{Solution:}

(1) As shown in Figure 1, when ray OE is above AB, $\angle BOE = \frac{2}{3} \angle COE$,

$\because \angle BOE + \angle COE = \angle BOC$,

$\therefore \frac{2}{3} \angle COE + \angle COE = 40^\circ$,

$\therefore \angle COE = \boxed{24^\circ}$;

(2) As shown in Figure 2, when ray OE is below AB, $\angle BOE = \frac{2}{3} \angle COE$,

$\because \angle COE - \angle BOE = \angle BOC$,

$\therefore \angle COE - \frac{2}{3} \angle COE = 40^\circ$,

$\therefore \angle COE = \boxed{120^\circ}$;

In conclusion: The degree of $\angle COE$ can be either \boxed{24^\circ} or \boxed{120^\circ}.
